                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "31570933",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198087811288",
                            "num_reviews": 2,
                            "playtime_forever": 110,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 110,
                            "last_played": 1494034878
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I will start with that I enjoy all the 'choice of' games I play so the recomendation comes from a general level of tolerance and enjoyment from these games.\n\nThis one in particular had a nice concept and fairly well presented story. \n\nWith that said I have just finished the game and boy does it have serious flaws that should be seen if you wish to purchase this game:\n1. It is very quick, it felt like I was jumping into experiences extremely quickly. I understand there is that constraint but it bounces through maybe 5 plot point over 3 days and then you're done.\n2. There is a lack of deeper lore and character backstory or maybe just less than I am used too.\n3. There are perhaps the wide range of customizables that are linked to these games but boy were they surface level.\n4. This is the last and most important, I don't know what motivation any character from the baseline would have in this whole thing, I just can't believe someone would act so rashly and completely.\n\nBuy if you like the concept and fancy a quick (less than 2 hours in my 1st playthrough) of a 'choice' game, otherwise if the price is to steep for that just leave it, probably end up just a bit disapointed like me.\n\n1st review so thanks for those that read this and I hope both the author and publisher move onto better things.\nPlease feel free to leave coments would be glad to discuss this or any of the other 'choice games, Thank You!",
